{"id": "sfmta-shop-rents-changed-by-word", "title": "Muni changed its shop tenants’ rent by word of mouth; the Board saw it years later", "seconds": 143.7, "voice": "elevenlabs:iPYqcpY8j8Ap4jUf28I3", "narrator": "Michael", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "f5cc76fd22544026", "words": 396, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["ls", "established[0]"], "text": "A 2019 lease the Board approved has one plain rule: any change must be in writing.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 5.36, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "ls", "kicker": "Executed lease, 44 Ellis Street, 2019 · Section 32.3", "text": "No amendment of this Lease or any party thereof shall be valid unless it's in writing and signed by all of the parties hereto.", "mark": "in writing"}, "emph": ["in writing"], "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.36, 0.77, 1.03, 1.14, 1.35, 1.8, 2.01, 2.22, 2.53, 3.47, 3.72, 4.37, 4.59, 4.72, 4.79]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[1]", "suspicious[1]"], "text": "The tenant is Tad’s, at 44 Ellis Street, in a transit agency garage.", "t0": 5.48, "t1": 9.9, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Tad’s, Inc.", "kicker": "44 Ellis Street, 5,368 square feet", "sub": "fixed rent; no percentage rent", "chip": "$36,905 a month"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.49, 0.67, 1.38, 1.56, 2.06, 2.32, 2.97, 3.1, 3.18, 3.6, 3.96]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[0]"], "text": "Fixed rent: 36,905 dollars a month, and no share of sales.", "t0": 10.02, "t1": 15.9, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Tad’s, Inc.", "kicker": "44 Ellis Street, 5,368 square feet", "sub": "fixed rent; no percentage rent", "chip": "$36,905 a month"}, "emph": ["36,905"], "wt": [0.0, 0.38, 1.25, 1.91, 2.45, 2.68, 2.94, 3.2, 3.48, 3.55, 4.26, 4.49, 5.01, 5.28, 5.38]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "span", "ref": ["timeline[2]", "suspicious[1].what"], "text": "Then, from 2021, the rent changed with nothing in writing. What did that change cost?", "t0": 16.02, "t1": 22.3, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2019-05", "to": "2021-01-01", "days": null, "fromLab": "lease approved, fixed rent", "toLab": "rent changed, no written amendment", "kicker": "The rent changes"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.4, 0.6, 0.87, 1.69, 1.86, 2.11, 2.57, 2.78, 3.11, 3.21, 4.57, 4.73, 4.84, 5.0, 5.3]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "suspicious[2]"], "text": "About 3.42 million dollars less rent over the lease.", "t0": 22.3, "t1": 25.54, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$3.42 million", "label": "less rent over the 44 Ellis Street lease", "sub": "approved retroactively in 2026"}, "emph": ["3.42 million"], "wt": [0.04, 0.32, 0.6, 0.87, 1.12, 1.36, 1.66, 2.01, 2.3, 2.57, 2.76, 2.86]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["bn", "story[2]"], "text": "In November 2025 the Board’s analyst reviewed another garage lease, for Mel’s Drive-In.", "t0": 26.16, "t1": 31.34, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "bn", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst · 5 November 2025", "text": "File 25-1052: Mel’s Drive-In, Fifth and Mission Garage", "mark": "Fifth and Mission Garage"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.58, 0.84, 1.47, 1.58, 1.94, 2.36, 2.77, 3.12, 3.5, 4.13, 4.3, 4.64]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[1]"], "text": "The agency told the analyst it verbally moved all its retail leases to eight percent of sales.", "t0": 31.46, "t1": 37.62, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "MTA reports it verbally amended all retail leases from fixed rent to rent based on eight percent of gross sales", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst, November 2025"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.63, 0.89, 1.01, 1.61, 1.94, 2.41, 2.82, 3.13, 3.28, 3.64, 4.45, 4.69, 5.02, 5.48, 5.58]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[1]"], "text": "About 50 leases were changed or forgiven this way.", "t0": 37.74, "t1": 40.13, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "about 50", "label": "leases changed or forgiven by word of mouth", "sub": "the agency’s count, as the analyst reports it"}, "emph": ["50"], "wt": [0.0, 0.3, 0.61, 0.95, 1.11, 1.54, 1.64, 1.96, 2.13]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "The analyst’s words: “The amendments were never documented.”", "t0": 40.25, "t1": 43.75, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "The amendments were never documented", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst"}, "emph": ["never documented"], "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.65, 1.57, 1.88, 2.36, 2.58, 2.92]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[1]"], "text": "And the agency has no written policies to govern its real estate.", "t0": 43.87, "t1": 47.57, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "MTA does not have any written policies and procedures to govern its real estate activities", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.26, 0.68, 0.97, 1.5, 1.83, 2.62, 2.77, 3.01, 3.15, 3.33]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why"], "text": "The Port, the Airport and the City Administrator documented their pandemic lease changes.", "t0": 47.69, "t1": 52.51, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "Port", "sub": "documented"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "Airport", "sub": "documented"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "City Administrator", "sub": "documented"}], "kicker": "Pandemic lease changes elsewhere"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.71, 0.86, 1.41, 1.56, 1.66, 1.93, 2.94, 3.41, 3.57, 4.09, 4.32]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "ls"], "text": "Back at 44 Ellis Street, the lease said it plainly: no percentage rent.", "t0": 52.73, "t1": 56.75, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "No Percentage Rent for this Lease", "kicker": "The 2019 Tad’s lease"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.31, 0.85, 1.1, 1.42, 1.57, 1.84, 2.05, 2.16, 3.06, 3.3, 3.76]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "timeline[2]"], "text": "From January 2021 the agency collected eight percent of sales instead.", "t0": 56.87, "t1": 61.14, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["the written lease", "$36,905 a month"], "b": ["collected from January 2021", "8% of sales"], "arrows": false}, "emph": ["eight percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.69, 0.97, 1.66, 1.84, 2.24, 2.68, 2.93, 3.25, 3.34, 3.71]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why"], "text": "Under the lease’s own terms, that deal did not exist until 2026.", "t0": 61.26, "t1": 65.18, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["the written lease", "$36,905 a month"], "b": ["collected from January 2021", "8% of sales"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.31, 0.66, 0.87, 1.35, 1.54, 1.81, 1.96, 2.11, 2.65, 2.93, 3.18]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "timeline[5]", "f500"], "text": "In June 2026 the change reached the Board, as a retroactive amended lease.", "t0": 65.4, "t1": 70.5, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "f500", "kicker": "Board File 260500 · Resolution 384-26", "text": "Amended and Restated Lease Agreement - Retroactive - Tad’s - 44 Ellis Street", "mark": "Retroactive"}, "emph": ["retroactive"], "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.5, 0.78, 1.41, 1.56, 2.06, 2.35, 2.45, 3.23, 3.42, 3.51, 4.2, 4.66]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[3]"], "text": "Retroactive, because the agency had collected the new rent since January 2021.", "t0": 70.62, "t1": 75.44, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "f500", "kicker": "Board File 260500 · Resolution 384-26", "text": "Amended and Restated Lease Agreement - Retroactive - Tad’s - 44 Ellis Street", "mark": "Retroactive"}, "wt": [0.0, 1.24, 1.5, 1.63, 2.04, 2.18, 2.56, 2.66, 2.81, 3.12, 3.4, 3.9, 4.2]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[3]", "suspicious[2].what"], "text": "It also forgave 332,145 dollars of 2020 rent,", "t0": 75.56, "t1": 81.49, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["2020 rent forgiven", "$332,145"], "b": ["water charges forgiven", "$65,400"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.46, 0.88, 1.13, 1.46, 1.93, 2.7, 2.93, 3.24, 3.78, 4.48, 4.64, 4.92, 5.21]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[3]", "suspicious[2].what"], "text": "plus water charges.", "t0": 81.49, "t1": 82.68, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["2020 rent forgiven", "$332,145"], "b": ["water charges forgiven", "$65,400"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.04, 0.46, 0.72]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[3]"], "text": "The 2019 lease would have paid 5,317,024 dollars. And the new projection?", "t0": 82.8, "t1": 89.68, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["2019 lease", "$5,317,024"], "b": ["amended lease, projected", "$1,899,144"], "kicker": "Rent over the term", "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.44, 0.87, 1.17, 1.34, 1.45, 1.71, 1.99, 2.37, 2.63, 2.98, 3.75, 5.25, 5.42, 5.54, 5.7]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[3]"], "text": "1,899,144 dollars.", "t0": 89.68, "t1": 92.89, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["2019 lease", "$5,317,024"], "b": ["amended lease, projected", "$1,899,144"], "kicker": "Rent over the term", "arrows": false}, "emph": ["1,899,144"], "wt": [0.04, 0.4, 0.75, 1.14, 1.83, 2.58]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["f500", "timeline[5]"], "text": "The Board adopted it as Resolution 384-26.", "t0": 93.31, "t1": 97.24, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "f500", "kicker": "Board File 260500 · Resolution 384-26", "text": "Amended and Restated Lease Agreement - Retroactive - Tad’s - 44 Ellis Street", "mark": "Retroactive"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.47, 0.87, 0.98, 1.2, 1.79, 2.06, 2.5]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[2]"], "text": "Did the Board have to approve? The agency says its 2021 change needed no Board vote.", "t0": 97.46, "t1": 102.83, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "We disagree with that interpretation and have requested the City Attorney’s Office to clarify", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst, on Charter section 9.118(c)"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.24, 0.52, 0.67, 0.78, 1.84, 2.03, 2.43, 2.68, 2.83, 3.08, 3.47, 4.25, 4.57, 4.79, 5.07]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "established[2]"], "text": "The analyst disagreed, and asked the City Attorney to clarify.", "t0": 102.95, "t1": 106.02, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "We disagree with that interpretation and have requested the City Attorney’s Office to clarify", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst, on Charter section 9.118(c)"}, "emph": ["disagreed"], "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.55, 1.37, 1.54, 1.73, 1.83, 2.07, 2.43, 2.53]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "The agency gave the analyst no record of the Director’s approval.", "t0": 106.14, "t1": 109.11, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "3 of 16", "kicker": "June 2026", "sub": "leases needing amendments, formally amended"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.54, 0.78, 0.9, 1.36, 1.65, 1.97, 2.03, 2.11, 2.53]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why", "established[4]"], "text": "By June 2026 it had formally amended three of 16 leases needing it.", "t0": 109.23, "t1": 113.41, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "3 of 16", "kicker": "June 2026", "sub": "leases needing amendments, formally amended"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.46, 0.74, 1.38, 1.47, 1.59, 2.0, 2.38, 2.76, 2.89, 3.4, 3.76, 4.03]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[4]", "innocent[0]"], "text": "The record gives reasons: garage traffic fell 40 percent, and the City urged tenant relief.", "t0": 113.63, "t1": 118.76, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Garage traffic fell 40 percent", "kicker": "The pandemic", "sub": "City Administrator memo, June 2020: give tenants relief"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.45, 0.75, 1.5, 1.85, 2.2, 2.45, 2.74, 3.39, 3.57, 3.67, 3.96, 4.3, 4.68]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[4]"], "text": "What is in question is the method: changes made without paper, approved after the fact.", "t0": 118.88, "t1": 125.19, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Garage traffic fell 40 percent", "kicker": "The pandemic", "sub": "City Administrator memo, June 2020: give tenants relief"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.38, 0.51, 1.3, 1.53, 1.64, 2.51, 3.09, 3.38, 3.72, 4.59, 5.49, 5.8, 5.91]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "Not known: who approved each change, and how much rent moved across all the leases.", "t0": 125.31, "t1": 130.3, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Whether the Board had to approve the changes", "Who approved each change", "How much rent moved across all the leases"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.28, 1.05, 1.25, 1.78, 1.99, 2.74, 2.9, 3.01, 3.22, 3.49, 3.9, 4.24, 4.43, 4.52]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it? The City Attorney’s answer, and the agency’s list of changed leases.", "t0": 130.42, "t1": 136.13, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "City Attorney", "what": "The answer on Charter section 9.118(c)"}, {"who": "Municipal Transportation Agency", "what": "The list of leases changed by word of mouth, rent owed and collected"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.37, 0.66, 1.78, 1.97, 2.27, 2.72, 3.43, 3.61, 3.74, 4.38, 4.7, 4.83, 5.23]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status", "notEstablished[3]"], "text": "No authority has found misconduct, and the City Attorney’s answer is not on file.", "t0": 136.25, "t1": 140.49, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.56, 0.69, 0.92, 1.75, 1.91, 2.01, 2.28, 2.69, 3.03, 3.2, 3.67, 3.87]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 140.61, "t1": 142.82, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.38, 0.77, 0.92, 1.18, 1.24, 1.33, 1.55, 1.8]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The lease", "lead1": "By word of mouth", "lead2": "In writing", "lead3": "After the fact", "lead4": "Who decides", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "midnight", "hook": "document"}